## Problem
The trust-critical tuning files are **not** listed in `.github/soundness-paths.txt` (kinds `file|glob|prefix|regex`, read by `_project/scripts/soundness_paths.py`). Only `benchbox/platforms/base/result_capture.py` is. Unlisted files:
- `benchbox/core/tuning/introspection.py`;
- `applied_ledger.py`;
- `capability_registry.py`;
- `metadata.py`;
- `platforms/*_introspection.py`;
- `platforms/clickhouse/introspection.py`;
- the corroboration code in `platforms/base/adapter.py`.

Changes to verification logic can therefore auto-merge without the external soundness review AGENTS.md requires.

## Change
1. **Preparatory refactor, no behavior change:** move `_corroborate_applied_ledger`, `_fold_layout_operations_into_ledger`, `_attach_applied_ledger_payload`, `_build_drift_check_payload` and the ledger read-back from `platforms/base/adapter.py` into a new module `benchbox/platforms/base/tuning_trust.py`. A manifest "region" is not expressible (plan review F8), and listing all of `adapter.py` would put most adapter PRs under soundness review.
2. Add manifest entries for:
   - `benchbox/core/tuning/introspection.py`, `applied_ledger.py`, `capability_registry.py` and `metadata.py`;
   - glob `benchbox/platforms/*_introspection.py`;
   - `benchbox/platforms/clickhouse/introspection.py`;
   - `benchbox/platforms/base/tuning_trust.py`.

## Guardrails (must preserve)
- The refactor is behavior-identical. The existing tuning unit and integration suites pass unchanged.
- This PR edits a manifest path itself, so it needs its own external `Soundness review:`.

## Do not
- Do not list all of `adapter.py`. That makes nearly every adapter PR soundness-gated; extract instead.

## Process guardrails
- One PR per item against `develop`, via the AGENTS.md worktree flow (`make worktree-claim BRANCH=...`, `make agent-write-preflight`).
- Verification ladder: `uv run -- python -m pytest -m fast -q`, `uv run -- ruff check .`, `uv run -- ruff format --check .` and `uv run -- ty check`.
- Then `make pr-preflight` and `make pr-open`.
- Stage explicit paths; never `git add -A`.
- No live cloud runs without explicit user approval stating the command, maximum runtime, log path and stop condition.
- Re-read every file:line anchor before editing. Anchors are from develop d39166ea.
